326 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (BIS, in its ongoing commitment to environmental protection and ecological conservation, has established the Environment and Ecology Department \(EED\) as a focused initiative to address the growing need for sustainable development. The EED is one of the 17 technical departments of BIS and has been recently constituted by consolidating various environment and ecology related standardization activities under a single dedicated division. This strategic move aims to streamline efforts, enhance coordination, and develop robust Indian Standards that support environmental sustainability, promote eco-friendly practices, and align with national and global environmental goals.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
